{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774878341,"nonce":"lQulNVOCEj7PTEsBPK3bTYTzKWI=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM74mnfp","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/28","origin":"github"},"title":"Refactor operator launch files to be generic across boats","message":"## Summary\n\nThe operator-side launch files (`operator_core_launch.py`) are nearly identical across boat packages (`izzyboat_project11`, `bizzyboat_project11`). Each duplicates the same pattern: UDP bridge + marine_autonomy operator core + foxglove + URDF publisher. The only boat-specific parts are the config file path, default robot namespace, and publish_state package reference.\n\nThis should be refactored so that `marine_autonomy` (or a shared package) provides a generic operator launch that each boat parameterizes with just namespace + config path, rather than duplicating the full launch file.\n\n## Current State\n\n- `izzyboat_project11/launch/operator_core_launch.py` — UDP bridge, marine_autonomy, foxglove, URDF, ros_tcp_endpoint\n- `bizzyboat_project11/launch/operator_core_launch.py` — same minus ros_tcp_endpoint\n- Both hardcode their respective config file paths and default namespaces\n- `operator_ui_launch.py` exists only for izzyboat (rviz + rqt), not yet created for bizzyboat\n\n## Proposed Approach\n\n- Extract common operator launch logic into `marine_autonomy` (or similar shared package)\n- Boat packages provide only: config YAML, default namespace, optional rviz/rqt config\n- Reduce per-boat operator launch to a thin wrapper or launch arguments\n- Consider whether `operator_ui_launch.py` can also be generic (parameterized rviz config + rqt perspective)\n\nPart of rolker/unh_echoboats_project11#14\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}